lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation complete, pushed as Gerrit change 1275 (commit e2c960417a, stacked on 1265/1262/1257).\n\nscripts/probe_rebar.py (623 LOC) replaces scripts/probe-rebar.sh (deleted in same change). Continue-on-failure preserved explicitly: assertion helpers count+continue (never raise), exit non-zero iff any fail; _show_json/_list_json degrade parse failures to {} / [] so a following assertion FAILS and the run continues (the jq-pipeline analogue).\n\nAssertion parity: all 140 shell assertions ported 1:1 by label, 0 retired. Side-by-side on the same build: shell 140/0, Python 140/0. Self-test PROBE_INJECT_FAIL=1: injected failure reported, run continues through all 19 sections, exit 1 (140 passed/1 failed).\n\nConsumers re-pointed atomically: test.yml:128 + gerrit-verify.yaml:209 golden-path steps (python scripts/probe_rebar.py), tests/unit/test_probe_wired_into_ci.py anti-rot substring (2 passed), docs/releasing.md pipx examples, external-integration.yml comment. jq dependency dropped from the probe. pyproject per-file T201 entries added for probe_rebar.py + check_config_reads.py (scripts/ legitimate-print convention; make lint scopes src+tests so the 6754 script had missed the list silently).","timestamp":1785728208785295001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patchset 1 Verified-1: golden-path job failed exit 127 (scripts/probe-rebar.sh not found). ROOT CAUSE: gerrit-verify.yaml executes from MAIN's workflow definition against the patchset tree — a change that deletes the shell probe can never pass main's still-shell golden-path step. Consumer sweep missed this executes-from-main dimension (4th consumer class beyond the 3 enumerated in-tree ones). FIX (patchset 2/3): restore scripts/probe-rebar.sh as a 7-line transitional exec shim delegating to probe_rebar.py; created d772-6007-5d04-4101 (discovered_from) to delete the shim once this change lands and main's golden-path step is the re-pointed Python one. Shim smoke-tested locally: 140/140. Patchset 3 fixes the shim comment to cite the real follow-up ticket id.","timestamp":1785730625293170001}],"created_at":1785640127838320001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1a803e6c-bb23-460b-832a-143f3f1a3cc8","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3342-e91b-19f9-49e6"},{"link_uuid":"0a719b81-45ba-4396-8684-97864a91f35e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"909e-2a9f-daf5-4dc7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nprobe-rebar.sh accumulated stale assertions (08ce: 3 stale asserts against removed flags/keysets). Its missing 'set -e' is DELIBERATE harness design (continue past failures, report all) — a naive port or hardening pass would break it.\n\n## Approach\nPort to a Python probe harness (scripts/probe_rebar.py) preserving the continue-on-failure design (collect results, report all, exit non-zero if any failed — the same contract, now explicit). Assertion-parity review required: every current assertion enumerated and carried over or retired with a reason (the 08ce class came from silent drift). Do NOT add set -e semantics.\n\nShell deletion and consumer re-pointing happen in the SAME change, after the side-by-side parity run: every consumer that hard-wires the shell path is re-pointed to the Python entry point in this change, so CI and the anti-rot gate track the new harness atomically.\n\n## Scope\n- scripts/probe-rebar.sh -> scripts/probe_rebar.py (port + delete shell)\n- Consumers re-pointed in the same change (enumerated by grep for 'probe-rebar'):\n  - .github/workflows/test.yml:128 — 'bash scripts/probe-rebar.sh </dev/null' -> python invocation\n  - .github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml:209 — same re-point\n  - .github/workflows/external-integration.yml:54 — comment mentioning the path; update wording\n  - tests/unit/test_probe_wired_into_ci.py — _PROBE_JOBS asserts substring 'scripts/probe-rebar.sh' in golden-path jobs; update the pinned substring to the Python entry point so the anti-rot gate keeps guarding\n  - docs/releasing.md:401,405,407 — invocation examples -> Python equivalents\n  - CHANGELOG.md + docs/experiments corpus jsonl are historical records — NOT touched.\n- Assertion inventory table in the change description (commit message).\n\n## Testing\nSelf-test: inject one failing probe -> harness continues, reports it, exits non-zero. Parity: run both harnesses against the same build before deletion, identical pass/fail verdict per assertion. tests/unit/test_probe_wired_into_ci.py green against the updated substring.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Python harness replaces the shell probe with continue-on-failure preserved.\n- [ ] Assertion-parity table: every shell assertion mapped to ported/retired-with-reason.\n- [ ] Side-by-side run shows identical verdicts; shell deleted in the same change with ALL enumerated consumers (workflows, anti-rot test, docs) re-pointed to the Python entry point.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/probe-rebar.sh","reason":"port to Python, then delete"},{"path":"scripts/","reason":"new Python probe harness"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","3342-e91b-19f9-49e6"],["relates_to","909e-2a9f-daf5-4dc7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"02bad0b9-b1cc-451c-b94a-530e08af4c44","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["shell-migration"],"ticket_id":"f1eb-5b53-f8bd-4f2b","ticket_type":"task","title":"Shell-to-Python Tier 2: probe-rebar.sh with assertion-parity review","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["89218e36-e642-4ce8-99d8-f14cac17ff58","51b1ddbf-406b-45d8-8269-e9c9d5e11da0","12c67998-7ca9-480e-99b4-404ed16c1827","5e5c1041-41b3-40a9-beeb-229f3823d4d5","02bad0b9-b1cc-451c-b94a-530e08af4c44","13bc7cf2-9066-415b-8fcf-e9c4009ec9e8","d43be572-b19a-4bc5-8ca9-2256312da136","1a803e6c-bb23-460b-832a-143f3f1a3cc8","f5a7da6e-91c6-4ec1-9048-958365c29abc","0a719b81-45ba-4396-8684-97864a91f35e"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785734861832323273,"uuid":"eae492f2-b6ad-4548-9830-dce910a46022"}